# Java build output
target/
# FND-82: the Maven wrapper. This was `.mvn/` + `!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar`, a
# negation that was dead TWICE OVER — git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, and `*.jar` below re-ignores it anyway. It mattered because the run scripts hard-
# require a system Maven (`command -v mvn` → "sudo apt install"), which on the locked-down
# corp demo laptop may need admin rights the presenter does not have; the moment someone adds
# the wrapper to de-risk exactly that, `git add .mvn` would have silently skipped the jar and
# the fresh clone would fail with `Could not find or load main class ...MavenWrapperMain`.
# Excluding the directory's CONTENTS (not the directory itself) is what makes a negation
# reachable; the wrapper jar is then re-included explicitly below the `*.jar` rule.
.mvn/*
!.mvn/wrapper/
.mvn/wrapper/*
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties

# Rovo/Forge (paused)
.wrangler/

# --- from GitHub's standard Java .gitignore template ---

# Compiled class file
*.class

# Log file
*.log

# BlueJ files
*.ctxt

# Mobile Tools for Java (J2ME)
.mtj.tmp/

# Package Files #
*.jar
# FND-82: must come AFTER *.jar — in gitignore the LAST matching rule wins, so this is the
# line that actually makes the Maven wrapper jar committable. The old negation sat above
# *.jar (and under an excluded parent directory), so it never had any effect at all.
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
*.war
*.nar
*.ear
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.rar

# virtual machine crash logs, see http://www.java.com/en/download/help/error_hotspot.xml
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# Claude Code session state and worktrees. .claude/worktrees/ holds EMBEDDED git
# repositories (a `git worktree` checkout is its own repo from the outer repo's point
# of view), so a plain `git add -A` stages it as a gibberish gitlink — a commit that
# looks like a submodule nobody can clone. Ignored so that cannot happen again.
.claude/

# Generated documentation index — regenerate with:
#   python3 ~/.claude/scripts/gen-docs-index.py <repo-root>
#
# Untracked 2026-08-05 after it was silently deleted from develop FOUR times. Two
# independent reasons it cannot be tracked in this repo:
#
#  1. RACE. push.sh's `wip: auto-commit` is a blind `git commit -a`, and the generator
#     rewrites this file by removing and recreating it. Commits landed inside that window
#     and recorded a DELETION while the file sat on disk with an mtime in the same second.
#  2. NOT REPRODUCIBLE ACROSS WORKTREES. Per-entry dates come from file mtimes, and the H1
#     is named after the containing directory — so each worktree legitimately generates a
#     different INDEX.md for identical docs. It was never going to stay clean.
#
# It is a derived artifact ("do not edit by hand" is its own first line) and regenerating
# costs one command, so tracking it bought nothing and cost four deletions plus a failed
# push. To go back: `git add -f docs/INDEX.md` and delete this block.
docs/INDEX.md
